BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-opening@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T091500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T093000
SUMMARY:Opening
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Mac Admins Europe 2026
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-session1@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T093000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T101500
SUMMARY:A Few of Our Favorite (Mac Admin) Things
DESCRIPTION:Armin and Rob will share a collection of tools\, tricks\, workflows\, and ideas that have made their lives as Mac admins easier (or at least more interesting). Expect practical insights\, unexpected discoveries\, and a few things you might immediately want to add to your own toolkit.\n\nSpeakers: Armin Briegel & Rob Potvin
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-sponsor1@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T101500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T104000
SUMMARY:Workbrew – Securing Developer Workflows (With the Tools They Already Love)
DESCRIPTION:Developers are often left to manage their own machines - installing what they need through Homebrew\, GitHub\, and increasingly via AI agents requesting additional tools on their behalf. This session explores how to secure macOS developer environments without disrupting how developers need to work.\n\nSpeaker: David Starr (Workbrew)
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-break1@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T104000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T111000
SUMMARY:Coffee Break
DESCRIPTION:Refresh and visit our exhibitors
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-session2@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T111000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T115500
SUMMARY:Do Mac Administrators Dream of Electric Users?
DESCRIPTION:We build elegant deployments\, polished scripts\, and "foolproof" workflows. And then... users surprise us. Borrowing ideas from psychology (and a certain sci-fi classic)\, we'll examine how users actually experience dialogs\, prompts\, and automated processes.\n\nSpeaker: Ulrik Aabye-Hansen
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-sponsor2@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T115500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T122000
SUMMARY:Jamf – Think Different. Then Update: Software Updates\, It's been a journey.
DESCRIPTION:Apple's software update ecosystem has evolved from manual updates to declarative management. Let's take a walk down memory to see how far we have come and where software updates is going.\n\nSpeaker: Rachelle Noel (Jamf)
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-lunch@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T122000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T132000
SUMMARY:Lunch & Networking
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy lunch\, visit exhibitors\, and connect with peers
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-specialguest@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T132000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T140500
SUMMARY:Special Guest
DESCRIPTION:More details coming soon
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-session3@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T140500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T145000
SUMMARY:Trust\, But Verify: Exposing Risk in Your App Catalog
DESCRIPTION:Every day\, our user communities request tools to improve their productivity. In this talk\, we'll explore techniques for inspecting the structure of mach binaries to make informed choices about the software we adopt and use.\n\nSpeaker: Alexandra Smith
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-break2@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T145000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T152000
SUMMARY:Coffee Break
DESCRIPTION:Last chance to visit exhibitors
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-sponsor3@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T152000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T154500
SUMMARY:Fleet DM – Unlock the future of device management with Fleet
DESCRIPTION:A practical look at Fleet's infrastructure-as-code approach to device management. Fleet's API-first design allows admins to control every endpoint management setting with version-controlled YAML files declaratively.\n\nSpeakers: Harrison Ravazzolo & Henry Stamerjohann (Fleet)
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-session4@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T154500
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T163000
SUMMARY:From Zero to Hero: Making Onboarding Magical
DESCRIPTION:First impressions are everything\, yet the initial setup is often a source of confusion. This session traces the evolution of macOS interaction\, showing how to move from legacy prompts to modern\, sophisticated dialogues using powerful tools like Setup Manager\, swiftDialog or Support App.\n\nSpeaker: Guillaume Gète
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mae2026-sponsor4@macadmins-eu.org
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T163000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Amsterdam:20260430T165500
SUMMARY:Iru – The Perpetual Promise of Passkeys & Passwordless
DESCRIPTION:We've been promised powerful and profound superpowers with a passwordless future powered by passkeys. What are passkeys? What do they do and why do we want them? Weldon Dodd from Iru will share principles and pointers to help power a pragmatic passkey provisioning project.\n\nSpeaker: Weldon Dodd (Iru)
LOCATION:Leidse Schouwburg – Stadsgehoorzaal\, Breestraat 60\, 2311 CS Leiden\, Netherlands
URL:https://macadmins-eu.org/program
END:VEVENT
